  "raw_text": "191\n\nPrais mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto put a price on, to assess\n \n/ poner precio, evaluar\n\nPraiskas\n \n–\n \nwithout value, priceless\n \n/ sin valor,\n \nsin precio,\n \nno tiene precio\n\nPrâk\n \n(Prak)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nshirt\n,\n \nrobe,\n \ngarment, piece of\n \nclothing\n, dress\n \n/ camisa,\n \nbata, prenda, prenda de vestir, vestido\n\n(\nConstruct:\n \nP\nr\nâ\nika\n;\n \nPrâmka\n;\n \nP\nrâka\n \n(\ndb\n,dictu,dict\n;\n \nPrâkka\n-\ndictu\n-\nalt\n)\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nAiseya\n \n36:22\n):\n \nai prâka nani ba kalkan\n \n–\n \nripped their clothing\n \n/ rasgaron su ropa\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb35\n):\n \nmani bani ...\n \nprisant baku pr\nâ\nk klahkla\n \nâ\npu raya kum yabi kan\n \n–\n \nevery year...(they) were giving a new sleeveless coat\n\nas a present\n \n/ cada año...(ellos) estaban regalando un nuevo abrigo sin mangas\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n05/20\n):\n \nJosep prâka maplira ba\n \n–\n \nJoseph’s colored\n \ngarment\n \n/ La prenda de color\nes\n \nde\n \nJos\né\n)\n\nPrâk dimaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto put a shirt on, to put a dress on, to put a robe on, to put clothing on\n \n/ ponerse una camisa,\n\nponerse un vestido, ponerse una bata, ponerse ropa\n\nPr\nâ\nk mahta\n \n–\n \nskirt\n \n/ falda\n\nLama pr\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nclothing to cover the chest, vest\n \n/ ropa para cubrir el pecho, chaleco\n\nPrakaia\n \n(v\n-\ntrans\n; in\ntrans:\n \nPrawaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto close, to unite, to cause to meet\n, to conclude\n, to block\n, to shut\n \n/ cerrar, unir,\n\nhacer que se encuentren, concluir, bloquear\n\nAikuki prakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto unite together, to join\n \n/ unir juntos, unirse\n\nAsla prakaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nAsla prawaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto join unitedly together, to stick together, to meet with\n \n/ unirnos,\nmanterneros juntos, reunirnos con\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb93\n):\n \nJisas ai disaipilka nani ra Galili ra asla prakisa\n \n–\n \nIn Galilee, Jesus meets with his disciples\n \n/ En Galilea, Jesús se\n\nencuentra con sus discípulos\n)\n\nDihbi prakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stock up, to pile up, to press together\n \n/ abastecer, amontonar, presionar juntos\n\nDur prakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto close a door, to shut a door\n \n/ cerrar una puerta\n\nKakma bara bîla prakaika\n \n(\ntkl\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nmask, something to cover the nose and mouth\n \n/ mascarilla, algo para cubrir\nla nariz y la boca\n\nLama prakaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsomething to cover the chest, shield\n \n/ algo para cubrir el pecho, escudo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-2\n \nSam\n \n22:3\n):\n \nyang Gâdki, kaini kahbi ba walpaya, yang laima prakaika\n \n–\n \nmy God, the rock protecting me, my\nshield\n \n/ mi Dios, la roca que me protege, mi escudo)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n09/20\n):\n \npr\nî\ns tara lama prakaika\n \n–\n \nbreastpiece of Israel’s high priest\n \n/ pectoral del sumo sacerdote\n)\n\nNakra prakaika\n \n(\ntc\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \neyelid\n \n/ párpado\n\nPrak alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto grab, to grasp, to grip\n \n/ agarrar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-1Timoti 6:19\n):\n \nPrak alkbia\n \n–\n \nto get a firm hold\n \n/ obtener un agarre firme)\n\nPrakaia bîla nani\n \n–\n \nconcluding comments in the Christian Life and Ministry meeting\n \n/ comentarios finales en la\nreunión de Vida y Ministerio Cristianos\n\nPrakaia bîla nani ba pain kaia sa\n \n(\nth\n-\n20\n-\ntit\n)\n \n–\n \nEffective Conclusion\n \n/ Hacer una buena conclu\nsió\nn\n\nPrakanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nclosure, union, conclusion, blockage\n \n/ cierre, unión, conclusión, bloqueo\n\nKaina prakanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nobstacle, …\n \n/ obst\ná\nculo, …\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata\n,\n \nPnata\n)\n \nprakanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nconclusion, ending\n \n/ conclusión, terminación\n\nYabalka prakanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nroadblock\n \n/ barricada\n\nPraki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto compare\n \n/ comparar\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nfy18\n):\n \nwal praki kaikisa\n \n–\n \ncompares with\n \n/ se compara con\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nAiseya\n \n40:25\n):\n \npraki ai kaikaisma\n \n–\n \nyou compare me\n \n/\n \nme comparas\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n07/21\n):\n \nD\nî\na muni Jehova upla wala\n \nnani wal praki wan kaikras?\n \n–\n \nWhy does Jehovah not compare us with\n\nothers?\n \n/ ¿Por qué no nos compara Jehová con los demás?\n)\n\nPraki kaikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncomparison, illustration\n \n/ comparación, ilustración\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-8\n):\n \nPraki kaikanka nani wal smalkaia\n \n–\n \nTo teach with illustrations\n \n/ Enseñar con ilustraciones)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nPraki kaikanka kum aisas\n \n–\n \nGive an illustration\n \n/ Dar una ilustración)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-03/20\n):\n \nJems ba dîa praki kaikanka yus munan?\n \n–\n \nWhat illustration did James use?\n \n/ ¿Qué ilustración\nusó Santiago?)\n\nPraki kaikanka isi\n \n–\n \nsimple illustration\n \n/ ilustración sencilla\n\nPura prakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto add, to multiply, to cover\n \n/ agregar, multiplicar, cubrir\n\nPura praki aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak in addition to, to exaggerate\n \n(hf)\n \n/ hablar además de, exagerar (hf)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nhf23\n):\n \nWahma bara tiara nani ba aima manis pura praki aisisa\n \n–\n \nYoung people often exaggerate\n \n/\n \nLos\n\njóvenes suelen exagerar\n)\n\nPura praki wiaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto say in addition to\n \n/ decir además de\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata, Pnata\n)\n \nprakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto conclude, to finish\n \n/ concluir, terminar",
